===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q198}}{{lb|en|uncountable}} [[organized|Organized]], [[large-scale]], [[armed]] [[conflict]] between [[country|countries]] or between [[national]], [[ethnic]], or other [[sizeable]] [[group]]s, [[usually]] but not [[always]] [[involving]] [[active]] [[engagement]] of [[military]] [[force]]s.
#: {{ux|en|[[holy war|holy '''war''']]; {{w|just war|just '''war'''}}; [[civil war|civil '''war''']]}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Exodus|1|10||Come on, let [[us|vs]] [[deal]]e wisely with them, lest they multiply, and it come to [[pass]]e that when there [[fall out|falleth out]] any '''warre''', they [[join|ioyne]] also [[unto|vnto]] our enemies, and fight against [[us|vs]], and so get them [[up|vp]] out of the land.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Mark|13|7||And when [[ye]]e shall [[hear]]e of '''warres''', and rumors of '''warres''', be [[ye]]e not troubled: For such things [[must needs be]], but the end shall not be yet.}}
#* '''1854''', {{w|Prince George, Duke of Cambridge|Prince George}}, letter to {{w|Sarah Fairbrother|his wife}} from {{w|Crimean War|Crimea}}:
#*: '''War''' is indeed a fearful thing and the more I see it the more dreadful it appears.
#* '''1864 Sept. 12''', {{w|William Tecumseh Sherman}}, letter to the mayor of {{w|Atlanta, Georgia|Atlanta}} & al.:
#*: You cannot qualify '''war''' in harsher terms than I will. '''War''' is cruelty, and you cannot refine it; and those who brought '''war''' into our Country deserve all the curses and maledictions a people can pour out... You might as well appeal against the thunder-storm as against these terrible hardships of '''war'''.
#* '''1879 June 19''', {{w|William Tecumseh Sherman}}, speech to the Michigan Military Academy:
#*: I've been where you are now and I know just how you feel. It's entirely natural that there should beat in the breast of every one of you a hope and desire that some day you can use the skill you have acquired here. Suppress it! You don't know the horrible aspects of '''war'''. I've been through two '''wars''' and I know. I've seen cities and homes in ashes. I've seen thousands of men lying on the ground, their dead faces looking up at the skies. I tell you, '''war''' is hell!
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1907|author=w:Edward Porter Alexander|title=Military Memoirs of a Confederate|pageurl=https://www.google.com.hk/books/edition/Military_Memoirs_of_a_Confederate/kuopAAAAYAAJ?pg=PA302|page=302
|passage=Here {{w|Robert E. Lee|Lee}} and {{w|James Longstreet|Longstreet}} stood during most of the fighting [at {{w|Battle of Fredericksburg|Fredericksburg}}], and it is told that, on one of the Federal repulses from Marye's Hill, Lee put his hand upon Longstreet's arm and said, "It is well that '''war''' is so terrible, or we would grow too fond of it."}}
#* {{RQ:Ford Life and Work|chapter=17|passage=Nobody can deny that '''war''' is a profitable business for those who like that kind of money. '''War''' is an orgy of money, just as it is an orgy of blood.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1935|author=w:Smedley Butler|title={{w|War Is a Racket|'''War''' Is a Racket}}|pages=1 & 7
|passage='''War''' is a racket. It always has been. It is possibly the oldest, easily the most profitable, surely the most vicious. It is the only one international in scope. It is the only one in which the profits are reckoned in [[dollar]]s and the losses in lives... Of course, it isn't put that crudely in [[wartime|'''war''' time]]. It is dressed into speeches about [[patriotism]], love of country, and "we must all [[put one's shoulder to the wheel|put our shoulders to the wheel]]," but the profits jump and leap and skyrocket&mdash;and are safely pocketed.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1941|author=w:George Orwell|title={{w|The Lion and the Unicorn: Socialism and the English Genius|The Lion and the Unicorn}}|section=Pt. III
|passage='''War''' is the greatest of all agents of change. It speeds up all processes, wipes out minor distinctions, brings realities to the surface. Above all, '''war''' brings it home to the individual that he is ''not'' altogether an individual.}}
#* '''1944 June 27''', {{w|Herbert Hoover}}, speech to the {{w|1944 Republican National Convention|Republican National Convention}}:
#*: Older men declare '''war'''. But it is the youth that must fight and die.
#* {{RQ:Orwell Nineteen Eighty-Four|chapter=1|page=7|passage=From where Winston stood it was just possible to read, picked out on its white face in elegant lettering, the three slogans of the Party:<br>'''WAR''' IS PEACE<br>FREEDOM IS SLAVERY<br>IGNORANCE IS STRENGTH}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=w:Norman Whitfield; w:Barrett Strong| title=[[w:War (Edwin Starr song)|War]]| album=[[w:War & Peace (Edwin Starr album)|War & Peace]]|artist=w:Edwin Starr| year=1969| passage='''War''', huh, Good God, [[y'all]]!<br>What is it good for?<br>Absolutely nothing...}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1997|author=w:Ron Perlman|title={{w|Fallout (game)|Fallout}}
|passage='''War'''. '''War''' never changes. The {{w|Roman Empire|Romans}} waged '''war''' to gather slaves and wealth. {{w|Spanish Empire|Spain}} built an empire from its lust for gold and territory. {{w|Hitler}} shaped a battered {{w|Nazi Germany|Germany}} into an economic superpower. But '''war''' never changes.}}
#* '''2013 July 20''', "[http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21581980-latest-research-suggests-humans-are-not-warriors-their-genes-after-all-old Old Soldiers?]", ''The Economist'', Vol. 408, No. 8845:
#*: {{w|E. O. Wilson|Edward Wilson}}, the inventor of the field of [[sociobiology]], once wrote that "'''war''' is embedded in our very nature". This is a belief commonly held not just by sociobiologists but also by [[anthropologist]]s and other students of human behaviour. They base it not only on the propensity of modern man to go to '''war''' with his neighbours (and, indeed, with people halfway around the world, given the chance) but also on observations of the way those who still live a pre-agricultural "[[hunter-gatherer]]" life behave... Whether modern, industrial man is less or more warlike than his hunter-gatherer ancestors is impossible to determine... One thing that is true, though, is that murder rates have fallen over the centuries... Modern society may not have done anything about '''war'''. But peace is a lot more peaceful.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[particular]] [[conflict]] of [[this]] [[kind]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1865|author=w:Herman Melville|title=The Surrender at Appomattox
|passage=All human tribes glad token see<br>In the close of the '''wars''' of {{w|Ulysses S. Grant|Grant}} and {{w|Robert E. Lee|Lee}}.}}
#* '''1999 Nov. 8''', {{w|Bill Clinton}}, speech at {{w|Georgetown University}}:
#*: A second challenge will be to implement, with our allies, a plan of stability in the Balkans, so that the region's bitter ethnic problems can no longer be exploited by dictators and Americans do not have to cross the Atlantic again to fight in another '''war'''.
#: {{ux|en|a {{w|war of succession|'''war''' of succession}}... a [[war of attrition|'''war''' of attrition]]... the [[Cold War|Cold '''War''']]... [[World War III|World '''War''' III]]...}}
# {{lb|en|countable|sometimes|_|proscribed}} [[protracted|Protracted]] [[armed]] [[conflict]] against [[irregular]] [[force]]s, [[particularly]] [[group]]s [[considered]] [[terrorist]]s.
#* '''2001 Sept. 20''', {{w|George W. Bush}}, speech before {{w|United States Congress|Congress}}, [https://web.archive.org/web/20090527194111/https://georgewbush-whitehouse.archives.gov/news/releases/2001/09/20010920-8.html White House Archives]:
#*: Our [[War on Terror|'''war''' on terror]] begins with {{w|al-Qaeda|al Qaeda}}, but it does not end there. It will not end until every terrorist group of global reach has been found, stopped and defeated.
#* '''2021 Sept. 8''', Seth G. Jones, quoted in Chris Moody, "[https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2021/9/8/20-years-after-9-11-did-the-us-win-its-war-on Twenty Years after 9/11, Did US Win Its ‘'''War''' on Terror’?]" ''{{w|Al-Jazeera}}'':
#*: "...These '''wars''' are not going away. This is at least a generational struggle."
#: {{ux|en|the {{w|Emu War|Great Emu '''War'''}}... the {{w|Global War on Terrorism|Global '''War''' on Terrorism}}... }}
