## {{lb|en|chiefly|_|US}} [[campaign|Campaigns]] against [[various]] [[social]] [[problem]]s.
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=w:William James|title=[https://www.uky.edu/~eushe2/Pajares/moral.html The Moral Equivalent of War]
|passage=The '''war''' against war is going to be no holiday excursion or camping party... Ask all our millions, north and south, whether they would vote now (were such a thing possible) to have {{w|American Civil War|our war for the Union}} expunged from history... and probably hardly a handful of eccentrics would say yes. Those ancestors, those efforts, those memories and legends, ar the most ideal part of what we now own together, a sacred spiritual possession worth more than all the blood poured out. Yet ask those same people whether they would be willing, in cold blood, to start another civil war now to gain another similar possession, and not one man or woman would vote for the proposition.}}
